---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CLARITY_ID, CONTACT_EMAIL, GA4_ID, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Legal notice of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: publisher, host and terms`} description="Publisher and host of the state labor law guide and its minimum wage, overtime, FMLA and final paycheck calculators; general information, not legal advice; governing law." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Legal notice' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Legal notice and terms of use</h1>
    <p>Information given under Article 6 III-1 of French law no. 2004-575 of 21 June 2004, the publisher being established in France.</p>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>Publication director: {AUTHOR_NAME}, responsible for the content of {SITE_URL}.</p>
    <h2>Host</h2>
    <LegalIdentity mode="hosting" lang={lang} />
    <h2>Not a government website, not a law firm</h2>
    <p>{SITE_NAMES[lang]} is independent. It is not run by, endorsed by or connected to the U.S. Department of Labor, the Wage and Hour Division or any state labor department, and it does not handle wage claims. Nothing on it creates a lawyer-client relationship. The pages summarize published statutes, regulations and agency guidance so that a worker can understand them; a person's own case can turn on facts the site does not know, such as a union contract, an industry wage order or the size of the employer.</p>
    <h2>Liability</h2><p>Each rule is read on an official page and dated, and the calculators are tested before each release, but laws change, sometimes in the middle of a year, and mistakes remain possible. The publisher is not liable for a decision taken on the site alone. Please report errors through the <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact page</a>.</p>
    <h2>Intellectual property</h2><p>Texts, design and code belong to the publisher; short quotations with a link are welcome. Statutes, regulations and agency documents quoted remain public records.</p>
    <h2>Embedding</h2><p>The worker rights calculator and the overtime calculator may be embedded for free with their credit link visible: see the <a href={route('widget', lang)}>embed page</a>.</p>
    {/* gen-legal-pages:terms */}
    <h2>Personal data and cookies</h2>
    {GA4_ID ? (<p>What you type in the calculators stays in your browser. The site sets Google Analytics audience measurement cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_{GA4_ID.replace('G-', '')}</code>, 13 months at most), with no advertising{CLARITY_ID && '; page stability is monitored with Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free'}. Details, legal basis and how to object: <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page.</p>) : (<p>What you type in the calculators stays in your browser and the site sets no cookies{CLARITY_ID && '; page stability is monitored anonymously with Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free'}. See the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page.</p>)}
    {/* /gen-legal-pages:terms */}
    <h2>Reporting unlawful content</h2><p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the address of the page.</p>
    <h2>Governing law</h2><p>French law applies; failing an amicable settlement, the courts of {LEGAL.jurisdiction} have jurisdiction. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
